   "text": "I read the drawing as a disulfide-cyclised peptide and wrote it out in sequence. I did not verify the SMILES with a parser. The stereo tags are my best reading of the wedges and hashes, so some may be wrong.\n\n**Macrocycle.** Two penicillamine (Pen) residues are joined by an S\u2013S bond. The ring runs Pen \u2013 Asn \u2013 Thr \u2013 7-methyl-Trp \u2013 Lys(N-acetyl) \u2013 Pen.\n\n**C-terminal tail from the right-hand Pen.** The chain continues Tyr(O-CH2CH2NH2) \u2013 2-naphthylalanine \u2013 1-aminocyclopentane-1-carboxylic acid \u2013 Glu \u2013 Asn \u2013 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxamide.\n\n**N-terminal side chain on the left-hand Pen.**\n- The Pen nitrogen is acylated by a Lys-derived residue whose \u03b1-nitrogen carries an isopropenyl group, N\u2013C(CH3)=CH2. I wrote this as drawn, although it may be a misdrawn acetyl.\n- The Lys \u03b5-nitrogen carries two repeats of an amino-PEG acetyl spacer, \u2013C(=O)CH2OCH2CH2OCH2CH2NH\u2013.\n- This is followed by a \u03b3-Glu unit whose \u03b1-nitrogen is acylated by an octadecanedioic acid (C18 diacid): 16 CH2 groups between the amide carbonyl and the terminal COOH.\n\nSMILES: C=C(C)N[C@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)O)C(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)NC2(C(N)=O)CCOCC2)C(C)(C)SSC1(C)C\n\nCheck on the diacid: that string has 17 C after C(=O), the last being the COOH carbon. That is one CH2 too many, so the correct fragment is NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC C(=O)O with exactly 16 CH2. The corrected final answer is:\n\nSMILES: C=C(C)N[C@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)O)C(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@